<title>HONG KONG: China Investment Bank mandates US$100 mln FRN.</title>
<headline>China Investment Bank mandates US$100 mln FRN.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>China Investment Bank has mandated five banks to lead manage a US$100 million floating rate note issue, bankers said Thursday.</p>
<p>The five-year notes will pay a coupon of 45 basis points over the London Interbank Offered Rate. With fees, the all-in return is expected to be in the low-50s.</p>
<p>Chase Manhattan Asia is lead manager and bookrunner. Other lead managers are Bayerische Landesbank Hong Kong, Daiwa Securities Hong Kong, HSBC Markets and Standard Chartered Bank.</p>
<p>China Investment Bank is a state-owned Chinese institution.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371</p>
